/" tabindex=3D"-1"><strong>Laura Wright</strong></a></h3><p class=3D"" styl=
e=3D"white-space:pre-wrap;"><strong>Ingredients<br><br></strong>Dressing</p=
><ul data-rte-list=3D"default"><li><p class=3D"" style=3D"white-space:pre-w=
rap;">1/4 teaspoon (2 mL) Meyer lemon zest</p></li><li><p class=3D"" style=
=3D"white-space:pre-wrap;">1 tablespoon (15 mL) fresh Meyer lemon juice</p>=
</li><li><p class=3D"" style=3D"white-space:pre-wrap;">1/2 teaspoon (2 mL) =
Dijon mustard</p></li><li><p class=3D"" style=3D"white-space:pre-wrap;">2 t=
ablespoons (30 mL) grapeseed or other neutral-flavoured oil</p></li><li><p =
class=3D"" style=3D"white-space:pre-wrap;">salt and pepper, to taste</p></l=
i></ul><p class=3D"" style=3D"white-space:pre-wrap;">Salad</p><ul data-rte-=
list=3D"default"><li><p class=3D"" style=3D"white-space:pre-wrap;">1 medium=
 head Romanesco broccoli (or cauliflower), borken up into florets</p></li><=
li><p class=3D"" style=3D"white-space:pre-wrap;">1 medium sweet apple, core=
d and chopped</p></li><li><p class=3D"" style=3D"white-space:pre-wrap;">1 s=
talk celery, small dice</p></li><li><p class=3D"" style=3D"white-space:pre-=
wrap;">1 cup (250 mL) seedless grapes, halved</p></li><li><p class=3D"" sty=
le=3D"white-space:pre-wrap;">3 green onions, thinly sliced</p></li><li><p c=
lass=3D"" style=3D"white-space:pre-wrap;">2 teaspoons (10 mL) minced fresh =
sage (about 1 sprig)</p></li><li><p class=3D"" style=3D"white-space:pre-wra=
p;">1/3 cup (75 mL) walnut halves, toasted and chopped</p></li><li><p class=
=3D"" style=3D"white-space:pre-wrap;">salt and pepper, to taste</p></li></u=
l><p class=3D"" style=3D"white-space:pre-wrap;"><strong>Instructions</stron=
g></p><ol data-rte-list=3D"default"><li><p class=3D"" style=3D"white-space:=
pre-wrap;">MAKE THE DRESSING: In a small bowl, whisk together the lemon zes=
t, lemon juice, Dijon mustard, grapeseed oil, salt, and pepper until combin=
ed. Set aside.</p></li><li><p class=3D"" style=3D"white-space:pre-wrap;">MA=
KE THE SALAD: In batches, use a food processor to blitz the Romanesco flore=
ts until you have a couscous-like size and texture. Place the processed Rom=
anesco in a large bowl.</p></li><li><p class=3D"" style=3D"white-space:pre-=
wrap;">To the large bowl, add the apples, celery, grapes, green onions, sag=
e and walnuts. Season everything with salt and pepper and toss to combine.<=
/p></li><li><p class=3D"" style=3D"white-space:pre-wrap;">Pour the dressing=
 over the salad and toss to combine. SErve the salad immediately or store i=
n a container in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.</p></li></ol><p class=
=3D"" style=3D"white-space:pre-wrap;">This delicious salad was part of our =
